    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "build from the ashes? what is there to build? the people i used to know won't even take my calls. my family looks at me like i'm a stranger. there's no \"new version\" of me. the version that mattered is just... erased. it feels like there's no point in even trying to fix something that's fundamentally broken beyond repair.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you—when the people who defined you vanish, the ground itself feels like it's gone. But \"broken beyond repair\" is a verdict you're handing yourself, not a fact. You don't have to rebuild the same man; you can build a quieter one, a stranger to the old life, who finds worth in small, unglamorous things. The point isn't to fix the wreckage—it's to learn to walk on new ground, even if it's shaky at first.",
